### Scenario 36 — Temporal saga state coverage
### IntelliJ HTTP Client syntax.
###
### Goal:
###   Cover Temporal-backed saga states:
###   COMPLETED, PENALTY_FAILED, AWAITING_PENALTY_APPLIED,
###   AWAITING_PENALTY_COUNTED, COMPENSATING_REVOKE,
###   COMPENSATED, COMPENSATION_FAILED.
###
### Prereq:
###   docker compose up -d kafka kafka-ui minio postgres-auth postgres-claim postgres-penalty postgres-temporal temporal temporal-ui jira
###   ./gradlew :auth-service:bootRun
###   ./gradlew :claim-service:bootRun
###   ./gradlew :penalty-service:bootRun
###
### Temporal UI:
###   http://localhost:8086
###   workflow id = penalty-application-{{saga_id}}
###
### Tip for manual timeout tests:
###   Set claim-service application.yml:
###     temporal.timeout-seconds.awaiting-penalty-applied: 10
###     temporal.timeout-seconds.awaiting-penalty-counted: 10
###     temporal.timeout-seconds.compensating-retry: 5
###   Then restart claim-service.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminEmail = admin@blps.local
@adminPass = adminpass
@landlordEmail = landlord@blps.local
@landlordPass = landpass
@tenantEmail = tenant@blps.local
@tenantPass = tenantpass

### 36.0 Resolve tenant id
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}

> {%
client.global.set("tenant36_id", response.body.id);
%}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Test A — COMPLETED
### All services must be running.
### Expected final saga state: COMPLETED
### Temporal history: penaltyApplied -> penaltyCounted -> markPenaltyCounted
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 36.A1 Create claim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": {{tenant36_id}},
  "title": "Temporal COMPLETED",
  "description": "Happy path saga should complete.",
  "claimedAmount": 100,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
client.global.set("claim36_completed_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 36.A2 Intake start
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_completed_id}}/intake-start
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.A3 Intake decision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_completed_id}}/intake-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestAdditionalInfo": false, "note": "ok" }

### 36.A4 Assessment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_completed_id}}/assessment
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "penaltyGrounds": true, "assessmentAmount": 80, "assessmentNotes": "completed path" }

### 36.A5 Tenant response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_completed_id}}/tenant-response
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "ack" }

### 36.A6 Support decision starts Temporal workflow
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_completed_id}}/support-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applyPenalty": true,
  "penaltyAmount": 80,
  "penaltyCurrency": "USD",
  "simulateFailure": false,
  "resolutionNote": "happy path"
}

> {%
client.global.set("saga36_completed_id", response.body.currentSagaId);
client.log("COMPLETED test workflow id = penalty-application-" + response.body.currentSagaId);
%}

### 36.A7 Re-run after 2-3 seconds until state is COMPLETED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sagas/{{saga36_completed_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.A8 Claim should become PENALTY_APPLIED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_completed_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Test B — PENALTY_FAILED
### All services must be running.
### Expected final saga state: PENALTY_FAILED
### Temporal history: penaltyApplicationFailed -> markPenaltyApplicationFailed
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 36.B1 Create claim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": {{tenant36_id}},
  "title": "Temporal PENALTY_FAILED",
  "description": "simulateFailure=true should close workflow as business failure.",
  "claimedAmount": 110,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
client.global.set("claim36_failed_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 36.B2 Intake start
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_failed_id}}/intake-start
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.B3 Intake decision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_failed_id}}/intake-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestAdditionalInfo": false, "note": "ok" }

### 36.B4 Assessment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_failed_id}}/assessment
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "penaltyGrounds": true, "assessmentAmount": 90, "assessmentNotes": "failure path" }

### 36.B5 Tenant response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_failed_id}}/tenant-response
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "ack" }

### 36.B6 Support decision with simulated penalty failure
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_failed_id}}/support-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applyPenalty": true,
  "penaltyAmount": 90,
  "penaltyCurrency": "USD",
  "simulateFailure": true,
  "resolutionNote": "forced failure"
}

> {%
client.global.set("saga36_failed_id", response.body.currentSagaId);
client.log("PENALTY_FAILED test workflow id = penalty-application-" + response.body.currentSagaId);
%}

### 36.B7 Re-run after 2-3 seconds until state is PENALTY_FAILED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sagas/{{saga36_failed_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.B8 Claim should become PENALTY_PROCESSING_FAILED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_failed_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Test C — AWAITING_PENALTY_APPLIED
### Manual action BEFORE 36.C6:
###   Stop penalty-service process only. Keep auth-service, claim-service,
###   Kafka and Temporal running.
###
### Expected immediate saga state: AWAITING_PENALTY_APPLIED
### If you wait past awaiting-penalty-applied timeout, it will move to compensation.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 36.C1 Create claim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": {{tenant36_id}},
  "title": "Temporal AWAITING_PENALTY_APPLIED",
  "description": "Stop penalty-service before support-decision.",
  "claimedAmount": 120,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
client.global.set("claim36_wait_applied_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 36.C2 Intake start
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_wait_applied_id}}/intake-start
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.C3 Intake decision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_wait_applied_id}}/intake-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestAdditionalInfo": false, "note": "ok" }

### 36.C4 Assessment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_wait_applied_id}}/assessment
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "penaltyGrounds": true, "assessmentAmount": 100, "assessmentNotes": "waiting for penalty-service" }

### 36.C5 Tenant response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_wait_applied_id}}/tenant-response
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "ack" }

### 36.C6 STOP penalty-service, then run this support decision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_wait_applied_id}}/support-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applyPenalty": true,
  "penaltyAmount": 100,
  "penaltyCurrency": "USD",
  "simulateFailure": false,
  "resolutionNote": "waiting for penalty-service"
}

> {%
client.global.set("saga36_wait_applied_id", response.body.currentSagaId);
client.log("AWAITING_PENALTY_APPLIED test workflow id = penalty-application-" + response.body.currentSagaId);
%}

### 36.C7 Run immediately: state should be AWAITING_PENALTY_APPLIED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sagas/{{saga36_wait_applied_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Test D — AWAITING_PENALTY_COUNTED and COMPENSATED
### Manual action BEFORE 36.D6:
###   Start penalty-service.
###   Stop auth-service process only.
###
### Expected immediate saga state: AWAITING_PENALTY_COUNTED
### Expected after timeout with penalty-service running: COMPENSATED
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 36.D1 Create claim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": {{tenant36_id}},
  "title": "Temporal AWAITING_PENALTY_COUNTED then COMPENSATED",
  "description": "Stop auth-service before support-decision.",
  "claimedAmount": 130,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
client.global.set("claim36_compensated_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 36.D2 Intake start
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_compensated_id}}/intake-start
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.D3 Intake decision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_compensated_id}}/intake-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestAdditionalInfo": false, "note": "ok" }

### 36.D4 Assessment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_compensated_id}}/assessment
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "penaltyGrounds": true, "assessmentAmount": 110, "assessmentNotes": "waiting for auth-service" }

### 36.D5 Tenant response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_compensated_id}}/tenant-response
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "ack" }

### 36.D6 START penalty-service, STOP auth-service, then run this
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_compensated_id}}/support-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applyPenalty": true,
  "penaltyAmount": 110,
  "penaltyCurrency": "USD",
  "simulateFailure": false,
  "resolutionNote": "waiting for auth-service"
}

> {%
client.global.set("saga36_compensated_id", response.body.currentSagaId);
client.log("COMPENSATION test workflow id = penalty-application-" + response.body.currentSagaId);
%}

### 36.D7 Run quickly: state should be AWAITING_PENALTY_COUNTED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sagas/{{saga36_compensated_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.D8 Run after awaiting-penalty-counted timeout: state should become COMPENSATING_REVOKE or COMPENSATED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sagas/{{saga36_compensated_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.D9 Run again after penalty-service consumes revoke: state should be COMPENSATED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sagas/{{saga36_compensated_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### Test E — COMPENSATION_FAILED
### Manual action BEFORE 36.E6:
###   Stop penalty-service process.
###   auth-service may be running.
###
### Expected:
###   AWAITING_PENALTY_APPLIED immediately after support decision.
###   COMPENSATING_REVOKE after awaiting-penalty-applied timeout.
###   COMPENSATION_FAILED after maxAttempts * compensatingRetrySeconds.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 36.E1 Create claim
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims
Authorization: Basic {{landlordEmail}} {{landlordPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": {{tenant36_id}},
  "title": "Temporal COMPENSATION_FAILED",
  "description": "Keep penalty-service stopped through all compensation retries.",
  "claimedAmount": 140,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
client.global.set("claim36_comp_failed_id", response.body.id);
%}

### 36.E2 Intake start
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_comp_failed_id}}/intake-start
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.E3 Intake decision
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_comp_failed_id}}/intake-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "requestAdditionalInfo": false, "note": "ok" }

### 36.E4 Assessment
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_comp_failed_id}}/assessment
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "penaltyGrounds": true, "assessmentAmount": 120, "assessmentNotes": "compensation failure path" }

### 36.E5 Tenant response
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_comp_failed_id}}/tenant-response
Authorization: Basic {{tenantEmail}} {{tenantPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "body": "ack" }

### 36.E6 STOP penalty-service, then run this
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/claims/{{claim36_comp_failed_id}}/support-decision
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applyPenalty": true,
  "penaltyAmount": 120,
  "penaltyCurrency": "USD",
  "simulateFailure": false,
  "resolutionNote": "compensation should fail"
}

> {%
client.global.set("saga36_comp_failed_id", response.body.currentSagaId);
client.log("COMPENSATION_FAILED test workflow id = penalty-application-" + response.body.currentSagaId);
%}

### 36.E7 Run immediately: AWAITING_PENALTY_APPLIED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sagas/{{saga36_comp_failed_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.E8 Run after awaiting-penalty-applied timeout: COMPENSATING_REVOKE
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sagas/{{saga36_comp_failed_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}

### 36.E9 Run after maxAttempts * compensatingRetrySeconds: COMPENSATION_FAILED
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/sagas/{{saga36_comp_failed_id}}
Authorization: Basic {{adminEmail}} {{adminPass}}
